A real chain as a server sends one: leaf, intermediate, cross-signed root. Captured 2026-09-16 with

openssl s_client -showcerts -servername www.google.com -connect www.google.com:443 </dev/null \
  | awk '/BEGIN CERT/,/END CERT/' > tests/data/chain-google.pem

Re-capturing gives a different leaf (Google rotates it every few months) and eventually a different
issuer, so the fields src/main.rs asserts come from this file. Nothing here is validated against a
clock: the tests parse, they do not verify.

